@startuml Cloud-Sync-Integration-Testflow
' Release: 3.8.1
title RAIkeep Real Cloud Sync Integration Test Flow

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam SequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam RoundCorner 12
skinparam ParticipantPadding 24
skinparam BoxPadding 16
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #fff7d6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #d4b106
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #64748b
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #f8fafc
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0f766e
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #ccfbf1
skinparam ActorBorderColor #1d4ed8
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #dbeafe
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #7c2d12
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #ffedd5
skinparam ArrowColor #9b2c2c
skinparam ArrowFontColor #374151
skinparam ArrowFontName "Casual"
skinparam DefaultFontName "Casual"
skinparam DefaultFontSize 18
skinparam TitleFontName "Papyrus"
skinparam TitleFontSize 28

actor Developer
participant "Nkosikasi\nmacOS\nTest Runner" as Mac
participant "RAIkeep Test Harness\nRemoteCloudSyncProbe" as Harness
database "Cloud Provider\nBackend" as Cloud
participant "Mzansi\nUbuntu\nSSH Observer" as Ubuntu
participant "PinovaP2\nWindows\nOptional Observer" as Windows
participant "Provider API Probe\nOptional" as Api

Developer -> Mac : Start real-cloud integration test
Mac -> Harness : Run scenario(provider, sourceNode, observers)

note over Harness
Recommended first scenario:
- source node writes file
- remote nodes wait for appearance
- verify content
- rename file
- verify rename propagated
- delete file
- verify vanishing
end note

Harness -> Mac : Create test id and source path
Harness -> Mac : Write file into provider root
Mac -> Mac : Record local write completion timestamp

par Cloud provider sync begins
	Mac -> Cloud : Local sync client uploads change
else Optional backend timing
	Harness -> Api : Query object visibility by provider API
	Api --> Harness : backend-visible timestamp or not-found
else Remote Linux observation
	Harness -> Ubuntu : SshFileProbe.WaitForFileContainingAll(...)
	Ubuntu -> Ubuntu : Poll local synced filesystem
	Ubuntu --> Harness : first-seen timestamp + content hash
else Optional Windows observation
	Harness -> Windows : SshFileProbe.WaitForFileContainingAll(...)
	Windows -> Windows : Poll local synced filesystem
	Windows --> Harness : first-seen timestamp + content hash
end

Harness -> Harness : Compare timestamps and content
Harness -> Harness : Persist propagation metrics

alt File appeared on required observers in time
	Harness -> Mac : Rename file
	Mac -> Mac : Record rename timestamp

	par Rename propagation
		Mac -> Cloud : Local sync client uploads rename
	else Linux rename observation
		Harness -> Ubuntu : SshFileProbe.WaitForRename(...)
		Ubuntu --> Harness : rename-visible timestamp
	else Windows rename observation
		Harness -> Windows : SshFileProbe.WaitForRename(...)
		Windows --> Harness : rename-visible timestamp
	end

	Harness -> Mac : Delete renamed file
	Mac -> Mac : Record delete timestamp

	par Deletion propagation
		Mac -> Cloud : Local sync client uploads deletion
	else Linux delete observation
		Harness -> Ubuntu : SshFileProbe.WaitForMissing(...)
		Ubuntu --> Harness : delete-visible timestamp
	else Windows delete observation
		Harness -> Windows : SshFileProbe.WaitForMissing(...)
		Windows --> Harness : delete-visible timestamp
	end

	Harness --> Developer : Pass with timing report
else Visibility timeout or mismatch
	Harness -> Harness : Capture provider, node, operation, timeout, paths
	Harness -> Harness : Capture local state, remote state, API state
	Harness --> Developer : Fail with diagnostic report
end

note over Developer,Api
Provider API checks are diagnostic only.
The real truth for RAIkeep is whether the synced file
becomes visible and usable on the other nodes.
end note

@enduml
